From: Nex package maintainers
Subject: system priority and deprecated PKCS#11 config readers walk the three UAPI tiers
Source: Nex downstream patch for GnuTLS 3.8.8
Upstream: not submitted; needs agreement on a machine-generated transient tier

GnuTLS compiles a single system priority file path, SYSTEM_PRIORITY_FILE
("/etc/gnutls/config" by default), and only honors GNUTLS_SYSTEM_PRIORITY_FILE
as an override. The deprecated PKCS#11 loader in lib/pkcs11.c reads a second
fixed path, "/etc/gnutls/pkcs11.conf", whenever GNUTLS_PKCS11_FLAG_AUTO
triggers the compat loader with a NULL deprecated_config_file, which is what
gnutls_pkcs11_init() passes on the first PKCS#11 operation. That reader is
live at runtime on this distribution because this package sets
--with-default-trust-store-pkcs11="pkcs11:", so ordinary trust store lookups
initialize the PKCS#11 subsystem and trigger compat_load().

Each reader keeps its own existing explicit override. The priority reader
still honors the GNUTLS_SYSTEM_PRIORITY_FILE environment variable, checked
first, unconditionally. The pkcs11 reader has no environment override; a
caller instead passes a non-NULL deprecated_config_file straight to
gnutls_pkcs11_init(), and compat_load() still uses that exact path without
running the new tier walk at all, because the walk is entered only when
configfile is NULL. Both readers keep the compiled no-file behavior
(compiled NORMAL priority defaults, no PKCS#11 modules loaded) when their
explicit override is absent and none of the three tiers exist. In that
unconfigured case, _gnutls_prepare_to_load_system_priorities() and
compat_load()'s NULL branch each now walk /etc/gnutls/{config,pkcs11.conf},
then /run/gnutls/{config,pkcs11.conf}, then
/usr/lib/gnutls/{config,pkcs11.conf}, and select the first path that is a
regular file. A present higher-tier file masks a lower one even if it is
empty or only restates NORMAL defaults, because the walk stops at the first
regular file, not the first file with content.

--- a/lib/priority.c
+++ b/lib/priority.c
@@ -2368,8 +2368,24 @@
 	int ret;

 	p = secure_getenv("GNUTLS_SYSTEM_PRIORITY_FILE");
-	if (p != NULL)
+	if (p != NULL) {
 		system_priority_file = p;
+	} else {
+		static const char *const tiers[] = {
+			"/etc/gnutls/config",
+			"/run/gnutls/config",
+			"/usr/lib/gnutls/config",
+		};
+		struct stat sb;
+		unsigned i;
+
+		for (i = 0; i < sizeof(tiers) / sizeof(tiers[0]); i++) {
+			if (stat(tiers[i], &sb) == 0 && S_ISREG(sb.st_mode)) {
+				system_priority_file = tiers[i];
+				break;
+			}
+		}
+	}

 	p = secure_getenv("GNUTLS_SYSTEM_PRIORITY_FAIL_ON_INVALID");
 	if (p != NULL && p[0] == '1' && p[1] == 0)
--- a/lib/pkcs11.c
+++ b/lib/pkcs11.c
